## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of Secrets Manager with a Lambda-backed API, rotation fundamentals, and validation of continuity.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets Manager secrets and rotation
- Least-privilege IAM roles
- Rotation Lambda workflow
- End-to-end testing without downtime

## Code Example
```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const sm = new AWS.SecretsManager();
async function getSecret(name){
  const r = await sm.getSecretValue({SecretId:name}).promise();
  return JSON.parse(r.SecretString);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle rotation failure and alerting?
- How would you extend to multiple environments (dev/stage/prod)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical AWS knowledge of private content delivery, CloudFront with OAI, and Lambda@Edge integration, plus a tangible test plan.

## Key Concepts
- CloudFront Origin Access Identity (OAI)
- S3 bucket policies restricting GetObject to OAI only
- TLS enforcement and viewer protocol policy
- Lambda@Edge for header augmentation
- End-to-end testing of CDN delivery vs direct S3 access

## Code Example
```javascript
'use strict';
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const request = event.Records[0].cf.request;
  const tenantId = (request.headers['x-tenant-id'] && request.headers['x-tenant-id'][0].value) || 'unknown';
  request.headers['X-Tenant-Id'] = [{ key: 'X-Tenant-Id', value: tenantId }];
  return request;
};
```

